
@1=~You wish to leave, I presume.~
@2=~(no response)~ 
@3=~Know that this door is mine. I control its opening and closing... A right of way is required to leave.~ 
@4=~What is the price to pay?~ 
@5=~A demon desires your sword. Give it to me.~ 
@6=~Retrace your steps. You will find a demon in a foul-smelling corner. Bring me its heart and I will let you pass.~
@7=~Very well, I will fetch what you ask for, but you'd better keep your word.~
@8=~Is this what you seek? (You show him the demon's heart.)~ 
@9=~I have no time to waste!~ 
@10=~In that case, find another way.~
@11=~In that case, come and take it from me. But this passage will be permanently closed...~
@12=~The simplest thing would be to bring me the heart of this demon in order to pay the toll.~
@13=~Magnificent, you have the demon's heart! I will be able to increase my powers!~ 
@14=~(He makes a vague arm movement towards the door). You may leave this place!~
@15=~No heart, no passage!~
@16=~Paying the price would have been so much simpler...~ 
// quest 
@100=~The Demon's Heart The Cambion tells me that he controls the gate. If I wish to leave this place, I must bring him the heart of the demon that is in the area.~
@101=~The Demon's Heart The Cambion tells me that he controls the gate. If I wish to leave this place, I must bring him the heart of the demon that is in the area. I brought back the demon's heart. The Cambion was delighted and announced that the passage was open after making a vague movement with his arm. I wonder if the passage had been clear from the start...~
@102=~The Demon's Heart I decided to go to the door, and it opened by itself. That Cambion tried to trick me into doing his dirty work.~
@103=~The Demon's Heart The Cambion told me he controlled the gate. If I wanted to leave, I had to bring him the Demon's Heart, which was in the area. I decided to open the gate myself. The Cambion didn't take it well...~
